<title>SOUTH KOREA: Sunkyong in $180 mln Cambodia forestry jv.</title>
<headline>Sunkyong in $180 mln Cambodia forestry jv.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Sunkyong Ltd said on Tuesday it had agreed to a $180 million Cambodia forestry development and wood processing joint venture with Malaysia's Samling Strategic Corp.  </p>
<p>A Sunkyong statement said it would hold a 40 percent stake in the venture and Samling the rest.</p>
<p>Sunkyong said the venture would offer a stable supply of wood products to meet rising domestic demand as the world's forest resources continue to decrease.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
